WEBVTT

00:00:02.790 --> 00:00:05.440
Another ensemble of mediocre programs, I see.

00:00:06.220 --> 00:00:09.310
Program proposals which do not adhere with Aikoh's rules and conventions...

00:00:09.310 --> 00:00:12.400
...are all rejected when they reach
the School Fair Committee Chair's hands.

00:00:12.890 --> 00:00:14.770
I understand, but...

00:00:14.770 --> 00:00:16.240
...this is so boring...

00:00:18.330 --> 00:00:19.060
What's this?

00:00:19.410 --> 00:00:21.200
It seems it got mixed into these documents.

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:25.230
That seems to be the papers the Seioh Student Council officer delivered yesterday.

00:00:25.230 --> 00:00:28.550
I'm sorry; it must've got mixed up when I was organizing the documents.

00:00:28.550 --> 00:00:30.210
A dodgeball tournament?

00:00:30.540 --> 00:00:32.090
I understand their aims, but...

00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:34.230
...what shall we do about it?

00:00:34.230 --> 00:00:35.400
Notify them of our absence?

00:00:39.470 --> 00:00:40.530
No, let's attend.

00:00:40.530 --> 00:00:42.020
This seems interesting.

00:01:04.790 --> 00:01:06.500
...and that's our piece.

00:01:06.730 --> 00:01:07.940
I'm so moved!

00:01:07.940 --> 00:01:09.400
Amazing!

00:01:10.210 --> 00:01:12.920
Then, can we leave these here?

00:01:13.270 --> 00:01:16.160
Okay! Okay! Of course, you can.

00:01:16.160 --> 00:01:17.570
All right!

00:01:17.570 --> 00:01:19.150
It was nice to be able to produce the CD,

00:01:19.150 --> 00:01:21.820
but we didn't know how to get others to listen to it.

00:01:21.820 --> 00:01:24.360
At this point, how about you make a jacket for it as well?

00:01:24.360 --> 00:01:26.540
Would you like us to put it on the Seioh website?

00:01:26.540 --> 00:01:28.720
Good idea, good idea!

00:01:28.720 --> 00:01:30.940
Load it up, load 'em all up!

00:01:30.190 --> 00:01:31.480
Excuse me...

00:01:31.820 --> 00:01:34.300
We're from the sweets society club...

00:01:35.380 --> 00:01:36.970
We wanted to ask a favor.

00:01:37.350 --> 00:01:38.320
May we come in?

00:01:40.090 --> 00:01:41.470
Yes, please.

00:01:41.960 --> 00:01:45.870
Two weeks have passed ever since the renewal of the Student Council Office.

00:01:47.120 --> 00:01:50.000
Look, turn around now

00:01:50.380 --> 00:01:54.340
but things like chances won't be there anymore.

00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:58.800
That's what some people will tell you,

00:01:59.390 --> 00:02:05.060
but there are just times when you can't move at all.

00:02:11.610 --> 00:02:14.530
Yes, everything I say

00:02:15.070 --> 00:02:18.990
is for your sake.

00:02:19.570 --> 00:02:21.490
Sorry, but

00:02:21.820 --> 00:02:23.780
I won't consent easily

00:02:24.040 --> 00:02:29.670
to things I don't accept.

00:02:31.330 --> 00:02:36.670
Even if I can get by that moment with a lie

00:02:36.670 --> 00:02:39.760
I'll end up regretting it afterwards.

00:02:40.340 --> 00:02:42.550
Whether it's the past or the future

00:02:42.550 --> 00:02:44.640
or, of course, the present,

00:02:44.720 --> 00:02:49.060
I am the one that has to shoulder it.

00:02:49.310 --> 00:02:53.730
You'll understand the meaning to everything afterwards.

00:02:49.310 --> 00:02:52.360
So let's worry!

00:02:53.770 --> 00:02:57.990
even if you don't understand them now,

00:02:58.280 --> 00:03:02.660
whether it has to do with pain, fortune or secrets.

00:03:02.740 --> 00:03:07.040
So don't cry, let's hold each other as we go

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:10.540
forever-

00:03:10.620 --> 00:03:16.300
It's My Life

00:03:10.620 --> 00:03:16.300
because it's my life.

00:03:14.960 --> 00:03:15.000
last fram of Manabi Straight! logo

00:03:21.310 --> 00:03:24.220
Listen carefully because I'm only going over it once!

00:03:25.020 --> 00:03:29.490
You should catch the ball by putting
your hands out and making your body round!

00:03:29.490 --> 00:03:29.980
Aye!

00:03:29.980 --> 00:03:33.550
When dodging, you should run in the direction of the opponent's dominant hand.

00:03:33.550 --> 00:03:34.480
Aye!

00:03:35.300 --> 00:03:38.230
Make them have to throw to
the other side of their dominant hand.

00:03:38.230 --> 00:03:39.850
That way, their reaction is slower,

00:03:39.850 --> 00:03:41.240
and the throwing power will decrease, as well.

00:03:41.690 --> 00:03:42.200
That's all!

00:03:44.150 --> 00:03:46.420
Mei-chan, you're so knowledgeable.

00:03:46.420 --> 00:03:48.380
B-Before you ask others,

00:03:48.380 --> 00:03:50.450
you should try to do your own research on the net.

00:03:50.960 --> 00:03:57.380
You guys are lucky that I just happened to, coincidentally, randomly walk past this room-

00:03:56.050 --> 00:03:57.750
'sup...

00:04:00.880 --> 00:04:02.810
I just happened to walk by here!

00:04:02.810 --> 00:04:04.300
That's all there is to it!

00:04:06.450 --> 00:04:07.620
Yo!

00:04:07.620 --> 00:04:08.690
Good job today.

00:04:08.690 --> 00:04:10.000
Helping out the softball team?

00:04:11.360 --> 00:04:12.320
Yeah...

00:04:12.320 --> 00:04:13.530
You don't seem too cheerful.

00:04:13.530 --> 00:04:14.470
What happened?

00:04:17.290 --> 00:04:21.620
Umm... well...

00:04:21.620 --> 00:04:23.860
Ehh?!

00:04:24.150 --> 00:04:28.510
Telling us now doesn't even give us enough time to find a replacement!

00:04:28.510 --> 00:04:30.220
We'll default our match at this rate.

00:04:32.180 --> 00:04:33.450
There's nothing we can do about it.

00:04:33.450 --> 00:04:37.400
Kanzaki-chan from the softball club has work that she can't miss tomorrow.

00:04:37.400 --> 00:04:41.770
In any case, we need to find another helper by today or else...

00:04:51.290 --> 00:04:52.630
Let me make this clear:

00:04:52.630 --> 00:04:55.690
I'm not the type of nice person that just likes to go around and help others-

00:04:57.550 --> 00:04:58.670
What are you doing?

00:04:58.670 --> 00:05:00.650
Make your body round when you're catching the ball!

00:05:02.320 --> 00:05:04.990
When dodging, you should run in the direction of the opponent's dominant hand.

00:05:06.700 --> 00:05:08.230
You don't have enough determination!

00:05:08.230 --> 00:05:10.160
Before the ball hits you, you should-

00:05:18.090 --> 00:05:21.810
And thus began our inter-school dodgeball tournament.

00:05:22.200 --> 00:05:24.830
We at Seioh planned the event...

00:05:24.830 --> 00:05:27.420
...and invited neighboring schools to participate...

00:05:27.420 --> 00:05:29.790
...in this inter-school dodgeball tournament.

00:05:30.150 --> 00:05:33.190
Fortunately, five high schools gave us the nod,

00:05:33.190 --> 00:05:35.670
and all gathered together at this place today.

00:05:41.250 --> 00:05:42.410
Umm, umm...

00:05:42.410 --> 00:05:43.690
To the opponent's dominant hand's side-

00:05:44.900 --> 00:05:46.350
What are you doing?

00:05:46.350 --> 00:05:48.320
When dodging, you should run in the direction of the opponent's dominant hand.

00:05:51.470 --> 00:05:53.410
Make your body round when you're catching the ball!

00:05:57.820 --> 00:05:59.330
You don't have enough courage!

00:05:59.330 --> 00:06:00.770
Before the ball hits you, you should-

00:06:02.240 --> 00:06:03.000
Ah...

00:06:29.990 --> 00:06:30.910
Here you go.

00:06:33.980 --> 00:06:35.410
Allow me to introduce myself.

00:06:35.410 --> 00:06:37.620
I am Aikoh High School's Student Council President,

00:06:37.620 --> 00:06:39.150
Kakuzawa Takako.

00:06:43.940 --> 00:06:46.370
Sorry about last time.

00:06:46.370 --> 00:06:47.630
Last time?

00:06:47.630 --> 00:06:49.680
You came all the way to our school, but...

00:06:51.560 --> 00:06:52.510
Ah.

00:06:56.870 --> 00:06:59.680
You created a very cute Student Council office.

00:07:01.160 --> 00:07:02.650
Thank you very much!

00:07:04.440 --> 00:07:06.780
I think the flyer for today was nice, too.

00:07:07.440 --> 00:07:10.110
All teams involve student council participation...

00:07:10.110 --> 00:07:12.280
...by requiring two members of the student council to be on the team.

00:07:12.280 --> 00:07:13.910
After the end of the tournament,

00:07:13.910 --> 00:07:15.910
we have planned for a social gathering.

00:07:17.510 --> 00:07:20.020
No one has come up with an idea like this before.

00:07:20.320 --> 00:07:23.280
By having all schools hold some connection with each other,

00:07:23.280 --> 00:07:24.970
we might be able to find solutions...

00:07:24.970 --> 00:07:27.590
...for the individual issues we have at our own schools.

00:07:28.740 --> 00:07:31.340
The purpose of this tournament was to create such an opportunity for us, right?

00:07:33.220 --> 00:07:36.810
I just thought that it'd be nice if we were all close to each other, I guess?

00:07:37.130 --> 00:07:38.400
Manabi!

00:07:39.090 --> 00:07:41.820
We ran out of ingredients for making yakisoba.

00:07:39.090 --> 00:07:41.820
Note: Yakisoba is Japanese-style fried noodles.

00:07:42.620 --> 00:07:44.230
I'll be right over!

00:07:44.950 --> 00:07:46.360
Talk to you later then.

00:07:46.910 --> 00:07:49.320
Good luck, Amamiya-san.

00:07:49.320 --> 00:07:51.200
Just call me Manabi!

00:07:53.080 --> 00:07:54.070
Manabi-san.

00:07:57.040 --> 00:07:58.740
Later then, Taka-chan!

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:01.030
Taka-chan?

00:08:15.870 --> 00:08:17.560
Is it really okay if I send you mail?

00:08:17.560 --> 00:08:18.470
Sure!

00:08:18.470 --> 00:08:20.650
Ah, tell me your address, too.

00:08:21.460 --> 00:08:22.850
Cheers!

00:08:24.410 --> 00:08:25.430
Ahem!

00:08:25.430 --> 00:08:29.400
Thank you all for making time
in your busy days and gathering here!

00:08:30.160 --> 00:08:34.670
This is our memorable 1st social gathering of inter-school Student Councils officers.

00:08:34.670 --> 00:08:38.250
Anyway, let us forget about
all the difficult issues we have!

00:08:38.250 --> 00:08:39.870
I think that if we don't get close first,

00:08:39.870 --> 00:08:42.310
we won't really have good ideas to give each other.

00:08:42.310 --> 00:08:48.000
So for today, let's just all eat delicious food and enjoy the day.

00:08:48.000 --> 00:08:49.480
What do you say?!

00:08:55.420 --> 00:08:56.630
H-Huh?

00:08:59.830 --> 00:09:00.850
Umm...

00:09:01.400 --> 00:09:04.440
Wasn't dodgeball enough for that?

00:09:05.250 --> 00:09:08.610
We all gathered here, so it's better
if we talked about something meaningful.

00:09:09.270 --> 00:09:12.310
Yeah, we didn't come here just to have fun.

00:09:11.110 --> 00:09:12.830
Oops.

00:09:12.310 --> 00:09:14.090
...was what I wanted to do.

00:09:13.580 --> 00:09:14.470
How maladroit of her.

00:09:14.470 --> 00:09:17.270
We need to make this about
something more meaningful.

00:09:17.270 --> 00:09:18.400
Right, right.

00:09:18.400 --> 00:09:19.680
Wh-What should we do?

00:09:19.680 --> 00:09:22.250
We didn't even prepare to talk about anything meaningful.

00:09:23.400 --> 00:09:25.400
Don't worry, Mikan-chan!

00:09:25.400 --> 00:09:27.040
Manabi-chan!

00:09:28.010 --> 00:09:29.920
Today's topic is...

00:09:30.800 --> 00:09:36.050
"What should we do to make campus life exciting and wonderful?"

00:09:39.390 --> 00:09:40.720
Exciting?

00:09:40.720 --> 00:09:41.680
Wonderful?

00:09:42.270 --> 00:09:43.470
What's that supposed to mean?

00:09:43.910 --> 00:09:45.280
How maladroit of her.

00:09:45.280 --> 00:09:46.620
Ehh...?

00:09:47.850 --> 00:09:48.730
Manabi-chan...

00:09:48.730 --> 00:09:50.330
I have no clue what she's saying.

00:09:51.280 --> 00:09:52.530
The School Fair.

00:09:54.540 --> 00:09:57.320
How about we talk about that?

00:10:00.280 --> 00:10:04.400
Timing-wise, every school should be in the preparation phase for this,

00:10:04.400 --> 00:10:07.240
so I believe it is a worthy topic for all of us to discuss, no?

00:10:10.500 --> 00:10:12.670
If Aikoh's president says so.

00:10:13.010 --> 00:10:15.360
Seioh's president is the one making the decision.

00:10:16.230 --> 00:10:16.840
Right?

00:10:19.590 --> 00:10:21.050
Let's go with that, then.

00:10:24.350 --> 00:10:25.480
In the end...

00:10:28.120 --> 00:10:33.120
In the end, Manabi-chan wasn't able to offer any suggestions.

00:10:33.820 --> 00:10:36.100
Despite that, with Kakuzawa Takako-san leading the discussion,

00:10:36.100 --> 00:10:38.790
the gathering ended up somewhat like a meaningful talk,

00:10:39.200 --> 00:10:42.020
but the student council officers social gathering ended like this...

00:10:42.020 --> 00:10:45.790
in a somewhat hard to digest fashion.

00:10:55.000 --> 00:10:57.050
Don't worry about it!

00:10:57.410 --> 00:11:00.350
It's just the way it ended up.

00:11:00.350 --> 00:11:01.740
Yep, yep.

00:11:02.180 --> 00:11:05.120
Dodgeball spiced things up quite well,

00:11:05.120 --> 00:11:08.160
so just be satisfied with the turnout for now.

00:11:08.770 --> 00:11:09.560
Ojisan, kaedama!

00:11:08.770 --> 00:11:11.760
Note: Kaedama is what one says when one wants another pack of noodles added.

00:11:09.910 --> 00:11:10.860
Me, too!

00:11:10.860 --> 00:11:11.760
You got it.

00:11:11.760 --> 00:11:14.070
Hey, you guys!

00:11:18.660 --> 00:11:21.420
A soy-sauce ramen please!

00:11:21.420 --> 00:11:22.150
Sure thing.

00:11:27.140 --> 00:11:27.920
Hot!

00:11:30.570 --> 00:11:32.790
So much for me worrying about you...

00:11:34.760 --> 00:11:35.670
Well then.

00:11:36.130 --> 00:11:37.760
See you then.

00:11:37.760 --> 00:11:38.800
Good night.

00:11:39.630 --> 00:11:41.020
Good night!

00:11:56.490 --> 00:11:59.140
The School Fair, huh?

00:12:28.790 --> 00:12:30.290
All right.

00:12:30.290 --> 00:12:32.100
Forward...

00:12:42.310 --> 00:12:43.920
You all seem sleepy!

00:12:43.920 --> 00:12:46.120
You were the one that got us up!

00:12:50.340 --> 00:12:52.590
Next station is Aikoh High School station,

00:12:52.590 --> 00:12:54.200
Aikoh High School station.

00:12:58.880 --> 00:13:02.220
Ooooo...

00:13:13.490 --> 00:13:15.540
If you read over those papers,

00:13:15.540 --> 00:13:18.990
you would probably have a good idea of what Aikoh's School Fair looks like.

00:13:19.690 --> 00:13:21.820
Just ask me if there's something you want clarified.

00:13:22.090 --> 00:13:24.720
I think I'd be able to answer most of your questions.

00:13:38.130 --> 00:13:40.180
Wow...

00:13:40.380 --> 00:13:42.600
Wow...

00:13:49.200 --> 00:13:52.010
Sorry for coming without any prior notice.

00:13:52.010 --> 00:13:55.690
No, I need to apologize for yesterday.

00:13:58.580 --> 00:14:02.040
You have your way of doing things,

00:14:02.960 --> 00:14:04.960
so I was worried if I was disliked for my actions...

00:14:05.720 --> 00:14:07.140
Of course not!

00:14:07.140 --> 00:14:09.850
We were able to get through it thanks to you, Taka-chan.

00:14:09.850 --> 00:14:12.090
You were our savior.

00:14:12.090 --> 00:14:13.530
Right, Mikan-chan?

00:14:16.520 --> 00:14:18.250
R-Right, right!

00:14:20.210 --> 00:14:21.200
Hello?

00:14:21.500 --> 00:14:23.040
She's in love, eh?

00:14:23.040 --> 00:14:24.460
She's in love.

00:14:24.460 --> 00:14:25.720
Hello?!

00:14:27.310 --> 00:14:28.820
So, what do you think?

00:14:28.820 --> 00:14:31.970
Did it provide you with any hints for your School Fair?

00:14:35.600 --> 00:14:37.350
I might've lost my confidence now.

00:14:38.940 --> 00:14:42.800
Your School Fair is so excellent.

00:14:42.800 --> 00:14:44.070
Yeah.

00:14:44.330 --> 00:14:48.380
It feels like we have a very high goal to achieve.

00:14:48.380 --> 00:14:51.260
We might not be able to do something like this no matter how hard we try.

00:14:51.680 --> 00:14:52.490
Hmph.

00:14:52.490 --> 00:14:56.300
The difference between the level of the schools and the numbers of students is too wide.

00:14:57.730 --> 00:15:00.300
Well then, we have our data now.

00:15:00.300 --> 00:15:01.340
So, let's leave.

00:15:01.880 --> 00:15:02.960
Right.

00:15:02.960 --> 00:15:04.490
It's bad if we intrude for too long.

00:15:04.490 --> 00:15:06.290
Thanks, Kakuzawa-san.

00:15:06.290 --> 00:15:08.010
U-Umm!

00:15:08.730 --> 00:15:13.510
I-I think you're a terrific Student Council President, Kakuzawa-san.

00:15:13.940 --> 00:15:16.390
W-We'll do our best not to lose to you-

00:15:16.390 --> 00:15:18.610
Ah, there's no way we'd win, but...

00:15:18.610 --> 00:15:19.510
We'll work hard...

00:15:19.510 --> 00:15:20.840
...and make it like Aikoh's...

00:15:20.840 --> 00:15:23.600
...and we'll organize a wonderful School Fair.

00:15:23.600 --> 00:15:25.970
Please come visit us then.

00:15:28.590 --> 00:15:30.260
Bye then, Taka-chan.

00:15:32.970 --> 00:15:34.160
Hey, wait.

00:15:41.550 --> 00:15:43.550
It's nothing...

00:15:45.250 --> 00:15:46.250
Good bye.

00:15:56.380 --> 00:15:57.880
Thank you, guys, for coming today.

00:15:57.880 --> 00:16:01.080
I might've felt a bit uneasy coming alone.

00:16:01.080 --> 00:16:03.400
Hey, don't worry; it was fun.

00:16:03.400 --> 00:16:05.350
It isn't something worth thanking for.

00:16:07.810 --> 00:16:11.840
Hey, what was Kakuzawa-san trying to say at the end?

00:16:12.180 --> 00:16:13.450
What, Mikan?

00:16:13.450 --> 00:16:15.290
You were wondering about something like that?

00:16:15.760 --> 00:16:18.660
Maybe she wanted us to pay for the coffee.

00:16:18.660 --> 00:16:19.670
I don't think so.

00:16:22.110 --> 00:16:24.200
What do you think, Manabi-chan?

00:16:30.050 --> 00:16:32.130
It's nothing...

00:16:32.570 --> 00:16:33.590
Good bye.

00:16:42.330 --> 00:16:43.520
I'm home.

00:16:44.280 --> 00:16:45.580
Welcome home.

00:16:45.580 --> 00:16:48.790
Tonight's supper is pork kimchi and green bean-

00:16:48.190 --> 00:16:49.120
I'll pass.

00:17:01.570 --> 00:17:03.250
Is she in a rebellious stage?

00:17:30.940 --> 00:17:33.590
For... ward...

00:17:34.360 --> 00:17:35.430
GO!

00:18:19.610 --> 00:18:21.060
That's right!

00:18:25.350 --> 00:18:26.640
M-Manabi!

00:18:26.640 --> 00:18:28.560
If there's something you want to tell me-

00:18:27.330 --> 00:18:28.560
Later, later!

00:18:34.760 --> 00:18:36.220
Eh, right now?!

00:18:38.870 --> 00:18:40.260
It can't be tomorrow?

00:18:42.950 --> 00:18:44.560
You can't say it over the phone?

00:18:46.140 --> 00:18:47.850
I'm sleepy...

00:18:49.770 --> 00:18:51.680
Tomorrow's too late!

00:18:51.680 --> 00:18:53.490
I want to say it right now!

00:18:53.490 --> 00:18:55.380
I can't express it over the phone!

00:18:55.380 --> 00:18:56.570
I beg you, guys!

00:18:57.290 --> 00:18:58.320
Get together...

00:18:58.820 --> 00:18:59.990
Get together...

00:18:59.990 --> 00:19:02.450
...at school!

00:19:04.690 --> 00:19:05.200
And?

00:19:05.750 --> 00:19:07.510
What are you going to do?

00:19:07.510 --> 00:19:09.140
Calling us out so late.

00:19:09.140 --> 00:19:10.320
I understand now.

00:19:11.380 --> 00:19:14.340
I understand what Taka-chan was trying to say.

00:19:14.340 --> 00:19:15.970
What she was trying to say?

00:19:16.450 --> 00:19:19.210
I think Taka-chan wanted to say this...

00:19:19.570 --> 00:19:23.230
That we can do whatever kind of School Fair we want.

00:19:23.810 --> 00:19:27.990
We can do an excellent School Fair like Taka-chan's school,

00:19:27.990 --> 00:19:30.900
or we can do something that isn't like that, too!

00:19:31.200 --> 00:19:33.320
And a School Fair that isn't like that is...

00:19:33.680 --> 00:19:35.240
I don't know yet.

00:19:37.050 --> 00:19:38.970
Let's all think about this together.

00:19:39.570 --> 00:19:42.780
Instead of just copying Aikoh's School Fair...

00:19:43.380 --> 00:19:46.410
...or striving to organize a school fair like Aikoh's...

00:19:47.160 --> 00:19:49.070
...let's make a school fair that we thought of!

00:19:49.070 --> 00:19:50.900
That only we can do!

00:19:51.430 --> 00:19:53.610
The one and only in the whole world!

00:19:54.610 --> 00:19:55.420
We can do this!

00:19:55.750 --> 00:19:57.760
There's nothing set yet!

00:19:58.080 --> 00:19:59.920
Everything's blank right now!

00:20:01.150 --> 00:20:02.270
Completely blank!

00:20:04.850 --> 00:20:07.430
That means we can do anything!

00:20:12.350 --> 00:20:14.450
We are the ones that will draw it out...

00:20:16.690 --> 00:20:18.780
...on this blank notebook...

00:20:22.910 --> 00:20:25.140
...the one and only in the world...

00:20:25.140 --> 00:20:27.500
...our own School Fair!

00:20:35.050 --> 00:20:36.320
Not by any one person,

00:20:36.900 --> 00:20:38.540
but by everyone!

00:21:06.950 --> 00:21:08.570
We can definitely do this!

00:21:23.050 --> 00:21:25.640
Our very own... eh?

00:21:26.520 --> 00:21:30.850
Weren't you just told to take this more seriously?

00:21:31.480 --> 00:21:35.600
But listening to her now makes us feel like we can accomplish this.

00:22:12.000 --> 00:22:17.300
We're still at the very beginning of things.

00:22:19.190 --> 00:22:24.050
Even the thousand-mile road starts with a first step.

00:22:26.660 --> 00:22:30.980
There's a first time for everyone,

00:22:31.190 --> 00:22:38.520
so take it on fearlessly - that's the best way to go

00:22:40.840 --> 00:22:47.800
I'm glad I chose a path I love,

00:22:48.000 --> 00:22:55.010
so thank you, God.

00:22:57.820 --> 00:23:03.310
I want to treasure my luck right now

00:23:03.530 --> 00:23:06.610
And stay happy on the way.

00:23:06.810 --> 00:23:10.450
Come on, let's ride on the momentum

00:23:10.710 --> 00:23:13.240
Bang！Bang！Bang！

00:23:13.300 --> 00:23:15.410
That's right, Lucky!

00:23:15.450 --> 00:23:19.000
Now is the time, happy!

00:23:19.060 --> 00:23:22.130
Grab your chances

00:23:22.210 --> 00:23:27.300
And live your lives to the fullest...
